SVG2GIF

Description:
svg2gif is a simple command-line utility that rasterizes SVG files into GIF images.
It uses the NanoSVG library for SVG parsing and rasterization and outputs indexed-color GIFs
with basic transparency support.

Features:
- Converts SVG files to GIF format.
- Supports transparency by detecting transparent pixels in the source image.
- Uses NanoSVG for lightweight SVG rendering.
- Uses giflib for GIF encoding.
- Outputs 256-color GIFs with dithered color quantization (grayscale or color).

Usage:
  svg2gif input.svg output.gif

Use '-' as output filename to write the GIF to stdout.

Dependencies:
- NanoSVG (https://github.com/memononen/nanosvg) for SVG parsing and rasterization.
- giflib (http://giflib.sourceforge.net/) for GIF encoding.
- Standard C libraries (math, stdio, stdlib).

Compilation Notes:
- Recommended to compile with no optimization (-O0) for stability on some libc setups.
- Link with -lm -lgif libraries.
- On uClibc systems, a math shim may be required to provide missing cosf and other float math functions.

Limitations:
- Does not support complex SVG features beyond NanoSVG’s capabilities.
- Optimization beyond -O0 may cause instability or crashes.
- Transparency support is basic, using first transparent pixel index.



